#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:115
msgid ""
"Mapping rules control Scouting OIDC login and the WordPress role managed by "
"this plugin. Rules are evaluated from top to bottom; only the first matching "
"rule applies. When no rule matches, the WordPress default role is used and "
"role mapping does not block login. The General Settings option for creating "
"new users still applies."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:116
msgid ""
"All selected conditions must match the same active SOL assignment. A user may "
"have multiple SOL assignments, but matching rules do not accumulate WordPress "
"roles. Independently managed WordPress roles are retained."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:117
msgid ""
"When Scouts Online supplies parent organisations, an organisation condition "
"also matches active assignments in descendant organisations."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:124
msgid "Adding and Editing Rules"
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:126
msgid ""
"Use Add Mapping Rule beside Test a User, or Edit on an existing rule, to open "
"the When / Then editor. Choose at least one organisation, unit or SOL role "
"condition, then allow or deny login. Allowed users receive the selected "
"WordPress role."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:127
msgid ""
"Search results update while typing. Searching retains the current selection; "
"choose a result to change it. Organisation and unit selections narrow "
"dependent choices. Arrow Down or Enter in a search field focuses its results."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:128
msgid ""
"Save or add the rule with the primary button. The close icon, Cancel and "
"Escape close the modal without saving. Without JavaScript or native dialog "
"support, the editor remains inline."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:135
msgid "Rule Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:137
msgid ""
"Use Move up, Move down or Position to change rule precedence. Put more "
"specific rules before broader rules when they should take priority. A later "
"deny rule does not override an earlier matching allow rule."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:138
msgid ""
"Duplicate appends a saved copy at the end and opens it for editing. Change "
"its conditions or outcome and move it if needed. Delete removes a rule."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:145
msgid "Testing a User"
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:147
msgid ""
"Test a User accepts an exact WordPress username or user ID. It shows active "
"stored SOL assignments, the winning saved rule, and the resulting login and "
"role decision."
msgstr ""

#: roles/class-rolesadmin.php:148
msgid ""
"The preview does not include unsaved edits, refresh provider data, change "
"user roles or sign the user in. If no rule matches, it shows the WordPress "
"default role. This previews role mapping only, not other login or new-user "
"registration checks. Updated provider data is synchronized during Scouting "
"OIDC login."
msgstr ""

